A||N||4||mrtgman||HELP! A/C BELT KEEPS BREAKING!||||8||
Z||000000||mrtgman||07-09-2001||02:21 PM||||I am on my third AC belt in three weeks. My mechanic and I are stumped. He is installing ac delco belts on the compressor and after 3 or 4 days they keep breaking or slipping off. Has this happened to anyone else and how did you resolve it?<P>Thanks||||reg||8
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-09-2001||03:31 PM||||Are you sure your compressor is running fine.  The guy I bought my fiero said that the a/c belt kept breaking.  That's because the a/c clutch was woking fine but the compressor was shot.  Everytime the a/c was turned on the belt would break.  Other than that I can't think of why this would be happening because unless the a/c bracket is bent to all hell the pulleys should be in alignment with each other.  Unless one of your pulleys are rusted or bent.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||07-09-2001||04:11 PM||||Does the A/C actually work before the belt breaks?<P>If so look at the belt and pulleys while it is running to see if there is a misalignment.  Maybe one of the upper compressor mounting bolts is missing (they are a pain to install) and allowing the compressor to move when the clutch is engaged.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||07-09-2001||04:37 PM||||Also check the pulley for any crud, build up, or anything in the V.<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||3
Z||000004||theogre||07-09-2001||07:43 PM||||There's really only a few things that would do it.<P>Compressor. It may be working but it may be on it's way out. An over charged AC system could push up load in the compressor as well.<P>Pulley wear/damage/contamination. Clean the pulleys with brake parts cleaner before putting on the new belt. Don't use anything that contains oil solvents on a belt/pulley. They ususally leave a film. The film can be enough to be a problem. After cleaning carfully inspect each pulley for damage and wear.<P>Pulley alignment.<P>Improper tension. Over tightening is as bad as loose. This reletively tiny belt can be a giant pain to get right. There's a tool some people here have tried that holds onto the compressor better when tightening the belt. Look like a big hook. That may be something to try.||||reg||1
